{{Quote|Well, ultimately, they will return, won't they, Colonel? When you need plenty of arms and legs to build all you've got planned.|[[Jayhold Beehaz]] to [[Colonel]] [[Soden Petigar|Petigar]], about the [[Dhani]]s|<ref name="Eye">{{Andor|The Eye}}</ref>}}
[[File:SeveredLimbs-2020DoctorAphra16.png|thumb|right|250px|The severed arms of various [[species]].]]
'''Limbs''' were major appendages on organic bodies, and could also be found on the mechanical bodies of [[droid]]s. Major limbs included '''legs''', '''arms''', '''hands''', '''feet''', and in some cases, '''wings''' or '''tentacles'''.<ref name="Bestiary">''[[Star Wars Bestiary, Vol. 1: Creatures of the Galaxy]]''</ref><ref name="AA">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref>

Limbs were often fragile and could be [[Dismemberment|lost]], such as after being struck with a [[lightsaber]]; [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] lost all of his limbs beginning with the [[First Battle of Geonosis]]<ref name="AotC">{{Film|II}}</ref> and ending at the [[Duel on Mustafar]], resulting in [[Cyborg|cybernetic]] replacements.<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> Years later, [[Luke Skywalker]] had his right hand cut off by Vader in the [[Duel on Cloud City]], resulting in a cybernetic replacement which had artificial skin.<ref name="Episode V">{{Film|V}}</ref> After the hand was hit by blasterfire, Luke covered it with a glove,<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> until abandoning it in his later years.<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref>

[[Trandoshan]]s were able to regrow their limbs if they were severed.<ref name="Scum and Villainy Case Files">''[[Star Wars: Scum and Villainy: Case Files on the Galaxy's Most Notorious]]''</ref> The [[Lasat]] [[Garazeb Orrelios]] believed that a being having more than two legs was "excessive."<ref name="The Mystery of Chopper Base">{{Rebels|The Mystery of Chopper Base}}</ref> In some cultures in [[the galaxy]], people were punished for theft by having a hand amputated.<ref name="Right-Hand">{{StoryCite|story=Right-Hand Man|book=From a Certain Point of View: The Empire Strikes Back}}</ref> The [[Scarif vault]] was cut off from the [[Scarif|local]] computer network and could only be accessed by a right hand-print scanner.<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> Some species could sometimes be born with a limb difference, such as the [[human]] [[Captain]] [[Fennro Drogan]]; one of his arms was shorter than the other and his hand had three fingers instead of four.<ref name="twitch">{{Twitch|video=1911875369|text=SWGOH KIT REVEAL - Captain Drogan|channel=capitalgames|name=CapitalGames_ExtraLife|date=2023-8-29|archivedate=20230830005209}}</ref> 

